    "notes": "Printed at line 140 as 2-chloro-3-methyl-4-sulfonylethylbenzoic acid, with the sulfone written backwards. sulfonylethyl names a divalent linker and cannot be a terminal ring substituent, so it is a transposition of ethylsulfonyl. The patent settles this itself: the Example 2 title at lines 136 to 138 prints the ethylsulfonyl order, and the printed 20 g charge with the 28.2 g product at 88% purity and 95.6% of theory closes only for the ethylsulfonyl substrate. The second alias is the EN normalisation printed at line 141, which silently repairs the name; it is a reading of the line and not a form the document prints."
